# CTrack Mobile Architecture

## System Overview
`ctrack_mobile` is a mobile-first PWA connected to `ctrack_v0` backend domain services.

- Client: Expo Router app (PWA-first)
- Backend: Next.js API routes + Supabase
- Data: Supabase Postgres with RLS
- Realtime: Supabase Realtime
- Media: AWS S3 (presigned uploads/downloads)
- Admin: Desktop control center in `ctrack_v0`

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  ArtistApp[ArtistMobileApp] -->|Auth + API| NextApi[NextApiRoutes]
  AdminWeb[AdminControlCenter] -->|Ops + Approvals| NextApi
  NextApi --> SupabaseDB[(SupabasePostgres)]
  NextApi --> Realtime[SupabaseRealtime]
  NextApi --> S3[(AwsS3)]
  ArtistApp --> Realtime
```

## Client Architecture
- Expo Router tabs: `Home`, `Work`, `Chat`, `Me`
- React Query for server state
- Offline cache + mutation queue for timesheets/reminders
- Shared UI primitives (`GlassCard`, `PrimaryButton`, `TimerPill`)

### Launch/Login Animation Architecture
- Add startup flow components:
  - `LogoSplashScreen`
  - `AuthLoadingGate`
  - `LoginScreen`
- Define a shared `BrandSpinner` primitive in mobile UI layer modeled after `ctrack_v0/components/ui/spinner.tsx` (`ctrack`/`modern` style)
- Use one animation system (`react-native-reanimated`) for:
  - logo reveal
  - spinner loop
  - auth state transition
- Enforce loading-state consistency: same spinner token set across splash, login, and data fetch placeholders

### Adaptive UI Architecture
- Build a responsive utility layer:
  - `useAdaptiveLayout()` hook for width/height class and orientation
  - `getSpacingScale()` and `getTypographyScale()` helpers by breakpoint
  - `isCompact`, `isStandard`, `isLarge`, `isTablet` flags for component branching
- Use `useWindowDimensions()` + `react-native-safe-area-context` for runtime layout
- Keep design tokens semantic (size tokens), not absolute pixel hardcoding
- Keyboard-aware layout strategy:
  - Chat input and action bars pinned with keyboard-safe offsets
  - Avoid fixed bottom offsets; compute with safe area + keyboard height
- Adaptive navigation:
  - Bottom tabs for phone sizes
  - Optional split/two-pane containers for tablet/large displays

